1
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja,
 
Yes, dear viewers,

2
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Vê carê jî me berê xwe daye navçeya Mabeta ne,
 
This time we have headed to the Mabeta district,

3
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
em ê bi hev re gundekî din nas bikin,
 
we will get to know another village together,

4
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
erf û adetên gund nas bikin.
 
and get to know the customs and traditions of the village.

5
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Em ê bi hev re derbasî xwezayê gund bibin.
 
We will go into the village's nature together.

6
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Du gund di vir hene,
 
There are two villages here,

7
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
ji vê re dibêjin gundê Kurka.
 
they call this the village of Kurka.

8
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Kurka Jorîn û Kurka Jêrîn.
 
Upper Kurka and Lower Kurka.

9
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Em ê bi hev re derbasî gundê Kurka Jêrîn bibin,
 
We will head to the village of Lower Kurka together,

10
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:27,000
em ê bi hev re vî gundî nas bikin.
 
we will get to know this village together.

11
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Merheba ser te.
 
Hello to you.

12
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Ehlen û sehlen.
 
Welcome.

13
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Em destpêkê te nas bikin?
 
Can we get to know you first?

14
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Navê min Hemadê ye.
 
My name is Hemade.

15
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Ser çavê min, birê Hemadê.
 
You are very welcome, brother Hemade.

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Îro em mêvanê we ne, mêvanê gundê Kurka ne.
 
Today we are your guests, the guests of the village of
Kurka.

17
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Me xwest em gundê we jî nas bikin.
 
We wanted to get to know your village too.

18
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Hinekî dîrok û taybetmendiya vî gundî nas bikin.
 
And get to know a bit about the history and characteristics
of this village.

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Du gund bi navê Kurka hene,
 
There are two villages named Kurka,

20
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
ev jî Kurka Jêrîn e.
 
and this is Lower Kurka.

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Em dixwazin hinekî navê vî gundî,
 
We would like to know a bit about the name of this village,

22
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
yanî destpêkê navê gundê we ji ku hatiye?
 
meaning, where did the name of your village originally come
from?

23
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Em xêrhatina we dikin.
 
We welcome you.

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Ser çavan.
 
Thank you.

25
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Hemû xebatkar û kameravanên qenala Ronahî.
 
And all the workers and cameramen of Ronahi channel.

26
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Û em zêde dilgeş in bi hatina we.
 
And we are very happy with your arrival.

27
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Ser çavan, ser çavan.
 
Thank you, thank you.

28
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Gundê me, gundê Kurkê Jêrîn e.
 
Our village, is Lower Kurk.

29
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Û Kurkê Jorîn, ev di bin, du Kurk in.
 
And Upper Kurk, these are below, there are two Kurks.

30
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Bi Kurdî dibêjin Kurk. Kurdiya berê.
 
In Kurdish they say Kurk. In old Kurdish.

31
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Yek li vir rûnişt, yek çû jor.
 
One settled here, one went up.

32
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Gundê Kurkê Jêrîn, gundê herî kevnar e.
 
The village of Lower Kurk, is the oldest village.

33
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Ji gundê Opê ya heya bi gundê Habo.
 
From Opê village all the way to Habo village.

34
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Û ji kevin de ew ava bûye,
 
And it was built a long time ago,

35
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
navê gundî Kurkan lê dihat naskirin.
 
the village was known by the name of Kurkan.

36
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Ji vê re digotin Herêma Kurkan bi giştî.
 
They used to call this the Kurkan Region in general.

37
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Ji kuderê heya kuderê?
 
From where to where?

38
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Ji gundê Opê,
 
From the village of Opê,

39
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Badîna,
 
Badina,

40
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Dimîla,
 
Dimila,

41
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
herdu Kurka,
 
both Kurkas,

42
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Sariya,
 
Sariya,

43
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Şêtana,
 
Shetana,

44
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
gundê Habo.
 
the village of Habo.

45
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Ev gund bi navê Kurkan lê dihatin naskirin.
 
These villages were known by the name Kurkan.

46
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Û dîroka gund, dîrokeke herî kevnar e di van gundên derdora
me de.
 
And the history of the village, is the most ancient history
among these villages around us.

47
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Yanî zêdetirî şeşsed sal heye.
 
Meaning it's more than six hundred years old.

48
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Naha navê gundê we,
 
Now the name of your village,

49
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
ji du zaro pêk hatiye ne?
 
is it made up of two children?

50
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Temam.
 
That's right.

51
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Dibêjin, yek li vir rûnişt û yek jî çû jor.
 
They say, one settled here, and one went up.

52
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Ê jêr nav lê dan Kurkê Jêr û ê jor nav lê dan Kurkê Jor.
 
The lower one they named Lower Kurk and the upper one they
named Upper Kurk.

53
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Ev kesane kî bûn?
 
Who were these people?

54
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Evana, em nizanin.
 
These ones, we don't know.

55
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Ji kevin de,
 
From the old days,

56
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
wek dîrokê û kal û pîrên...
 
like history and the elders who...

57
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
ev ji me re, dîroka xebardan e eve.
 
they told us this history, this is it.

58
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Hîn di nav devkî tê gotin?
 
Are there still any spoken verbally?

59
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Kes nas nake, nizanin.
 
No one recognizes it, they don't know.

60
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Kesî nizanibû.
 
No one knew.

61
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Kesî nedizanibû.
 
No one knew.

62
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Bes dîrok, pir tişt hene ispat dikin,
 
But history, there are many things that prove,

63
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,000
zêdetirî şeşsed sal e ev gund ava bûye.
 
it's been over six hundred years since this village was
built.

64
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Kerem ke, wek çi hene?
 
Go ahead, like what?

65
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Wek pir hene mesela,
 
For example, there are many,

66
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,000
tu kanî deh bava, bihejmêrî ku li vî gundî bî.
 
you can count ten generations, that have been in this
village.

67
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:51,000
E deh bavên ku te behs kirî çiqas sal derbas dike.
 
If you mention ten generations, how many years pass?

68
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Pir derbas dike.
 
A lot pass.

69
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Û gund, ji ber xwe, ji neh malbatan ava bûye.
 
And the village itself, was built by nine families.

70
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Malbatên, herî sereke ew ku digotin mala Hemît e.
 
The most prominent families, the one they called the Hemît
family.

71
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Mala Hemît yê Kurkê bi xwe bûn.
 
The Hemît family were from Kurk itself.

72
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Li ser Ereban, derekî çêtir a wî hebû,
 
Over the Arabs, he had a better place,

73
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
çû ser çinarê ket xwarê,
 
he went on the plane tree and fell down,

74
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
jê ket mir.
 
he fell from it and died.

75
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Ji ber vê qehirîn,
 
Because of this they were devastated,

76
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
di wê demê de tiştê ku hebûn,
 
at that time, whatever they had,

77
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,000
gişt kom kir, û agir berdanê û dev ji gund berdan û çûn.
 
they gathered it all, set it on fire, abandoned the village
and left.

78
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Ku da çûn?
 
Where did they go?

79
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Em nizanin ku da çûn e.
 
We don't know where they went.

80
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Çûn.
 
They left.

81
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Çûn.
 
They left.

82
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Na kes nizane ku da çûn e.
 
No, no one knows where they went.

83
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Bes lawikê xwe hebû,
 
He only had a son,

84
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
keserê cem anî dîn,
 
the sorrow drove him crazy,

85
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,000
ji ber wî koçber bûn û çûn. Tiştê xwe gişt şewitandin, li
vir nehiştin.
 
because of him they migrated and left. They burned all their
belongings, they left nothing here.

86
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Û xanî jî berî vê demê, ku bîst û pênc sal, sîh sal e, dema
ku ev erd hat kolandin,
 
And the house too, before this time, 25 to 30 years ago,
when this land was dug,

87
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:47,000
ispat kir, heta kevrê çêkirinê, gişk reş bibû, wate
şewitandibûn.
 
it was proven, even the building stones had turned
completely black, meaning they had burned it.

88
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Hat ispatkirin ku di wan xaniyan de ev kar hatibû kirin.
 
It was proven that in those houses, this had been done.

89
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Ev malbatên din?
 
What about the other families?

90
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Malbatên din,
 
The other families,

91
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
yek jê re dibêjin Altanan.
 
one of them is called Altanan.

92
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Ewana ji deşta Hemqê hatin e.
 
They came from the plain of Hemq.

93
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Hatin, li rojavayê gund rûniştin, piştî wê hatin li gund ava
kirin.
 
They came, settled in the west of the village, after that
they came and built up the village.

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Malên Hemdûç e, ev serek e di malên Hemdûç e û ê malên
Hemdûç e,
 
The Hemdûç families, this is the head of the Hemdûç families
and the Hemdûç families,

95
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
evna hatin li gund ava kirin û piştî wî em hatin.
 
these came and built the village and after him we came.

96
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
Mala Kurê Ehmed e hatin.
 
The Kurê Ehmed family came.

97
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Malên Orgît e hatin.
 
The Orgît family came.

98
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Malên Orgît e, Kurê Ehmed e, ji Badîna hatin.
 
The Orgît family, the Kurê Ehmed family, came from Badîna.

99
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Orgîtan ji Başûrê Dimîla hatin, gund ava kirin.
 
The Orgît family came from South Dimila, and built the
village.

100
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Malên Evdêkê ji Kobanê hatin.
 
The Evdêkê family came from Kobanê.

101
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Bapîrê Kurka, li Başûrê Dimîla bûn.
 
The ancestors of Kurka, were in South Dimila.

102
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Mala Evdêkê ji Kobaniyê hatin.
 
The Evdêkê family came from Kobanê.

103
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Ew jî ji eşîra Naîmî ne. Eşîra wan jî eşîra Naîmî ne.
 
They are also from the Naîmî tribe. Their tribe is the Naîmî
tribe.

104
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Cem yek hebû, hat meletiya xwe kir, bû xoce,
 
There was a community that had one, he came and served as a
cleric, he became a teacher,

105
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
û li vir jî zewicî, û li vir cîgirt, ew jî Rûbarî bû.
 
and he married here, and he settled here, he was also from
Rûbar.

106
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Ew jî ji heştê salî vir da, li vir rûniştiye.
 
He has also been living here for about eighty years.

107
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Ji kîjan gundî?
 
From which village?

108
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Ji gundê Bînê.
 
From the village of Bînê.

109
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
Ji gundê Bînê.
 
From the village of Bînê.

110
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Ji gundê Bînê.
 
From the village of Bînê.

111
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Û mala Têwo da hene, ew jî ji deşta Hemqê hatin e,
 
And there is the Têwo family, they also came from the plain
of Hemq,

112
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
bes, li vir barkirin çûn.
 
but, they moved away from here.

113
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Yek jê çû Efrînê, û yê din jî hindan e, ku da çûne em
nizanin.
 
One of them went to Afrin, and the others are lost, we don't
know where they went.

114
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Mala Elî Şêrvîn hene.
 
There is the Elî Şêrvîn family.

115
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Elî Şêrvîn jî û mala Eynê, ev jî ji vî gundî bûn.
 
Elî Şêrvîn too, and the Eynê family, they were also from
this village.

116
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Şert û mercên wê demê çi bûn, mala Elî Şêrvîn ji Kobanê
hatibûn.
 
Whatever the conditions were at that time, the Elî Şêrvîn
family had come from Kobanê.

117
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Ew jî li vir ava bûn.
 
They also settled here.

118
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Şert û merc çêbûn, derfet çêbûn, rabûn, her yekî çû gundekî.
 
Conditions happened, circumstances arose, they got up, each
went to a village.

119
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Hin çûn Kurkê Jorîn, û hin jî çûn Dimîla.
 
Some went to Upper Kurk, and some also went to Dimila.

120
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Mala Eynê jî çûn navçeya Raco gundê Moseka.
 
The Eynê family also went to the Raco district, to the
village of Moseka.

121
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Naha, gundê we çend xanî tê da hene?
 
Now, how many houses are there in your village?

122
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Gundê me حeftê û pênc xanî tê da hene.
 
Our village has seventy-five houses in it.

123
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Pêncî malbat di hundirê Sûriyê de mane, xêrî vî gundî.
 
Fifty families have remained inside Syria, other than this
village.

124
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Û sed û pêncî malbat jî derketin derve.
 
And a hundred and fifty families have gone abroad.

125
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Çûn Libnanê, çûn Ewrûpa, çûn Tirkiye, evna çûn.
 
They went to Lebanon, they went to Europe, they went to
Turkey, these went.

126
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Ew pêncî malbat yanî di nava Efrîn û Helebê de ne?
 
Those fifty families, meaning they are between Afrin and
Aleppo?

127
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Di Efrîn û Helebê de û li Şamê de. Di vir de mane, ên din jî
derketin derva, kes li vir nema ye.
 
In Afrin, in Aleppo, and in Damascus. They stayed here, the
others went abroad, nobody stayed here.

128
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Ê Kurê Ehmed, e... sala hezar û heştsed û şêst û pênca,
 
The Kurê Ehmed, uh... in the year eighteen sixty-five,

129
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Mihemed Axê hebû, xwedî kêl û bî... hat li vî derê mehsere
girt û mehsere ava kir.
 
There was Mihemed Axa, he had standing... he came here and
took a press and built the press.

130
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Dema mehsere ava kir,
 
When he built the press,

131
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:30,000
ji vî derê yek bir, du bira hatin li vir rûniştin.
 
he brought one from here, two brothers came and settled
here.

132
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Yek Hesen Axa yek Heyder Axa.
 
One Hesen Axa, one Heyder Axa.

133
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Hesen Axa li vir rûnişt, Heyder Axa li Kurkê Jorîn rûnişt.
 
Hesen Axa settled here, Heyder Axa settled in Upper Kurk.

134
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Heyder Axa xwest ji vira, Hesen Axa xwest ji Badîna.
 
Heyder Axa requested from here, Hesen Axa requested from
Badîna.

135
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Tekra têkçûnek... xilaf çêbû,
 
Again a breakdown... a disagreement happened,

136
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Heyder Axa daxwist jêr, Hesen Axa birin Kurkê Jor.
 
Heyder Axa requested the lower one, they took Hesen Axa to
Upper Kurk.

137
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Gotin, ya Kurkê Jêrîn e, girîng e tu li Kurkê Jêrîn bî,
 
They said, it's Lower Kurk, it's important that you are in
Lower Kurk,

138
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
û Hesen Axa jî, li Kurkê Jorîn be.
 
and Hesen Axa too, should be in Upper Kurk.

139
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Û di nav de jî, gundên... pir tiştên baş hebûn.
 
And in between, the villages... there were many good things.

140
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Çiqas, tiştên nabaş çêdibûn, rûspiyê me hebûn,
 
Whenever, bad things would happen, we had elders,

141
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:13,000
diketin navê, ew tişt çareser dikirin û kesî gilî û gazinc
nedikir ji hevdu, wek bira di nav hev de dijiyan.
 
they would step in, they would resolve those issues and no
one would complain about each other, they lived like
brothers among each other.

142
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Naha di navbera gundê we û gundê Kurkê Jor de...
 
Now, between your village and the village of Upper Kurk...

143
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
wilo merivatiyek heye?
 
is there a kinship like that?

144
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Welleh, bingehek heye.
 
By God, there is a foundation.

145
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Bes tu merivatî ji hevdu re nekirine, yanî keç û jin kesî
nedaye hevdu,
 
But they haven't created any kinship with each other,
meaning no one has given girls or women to each other,

146
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:30,000
û ne birine û ne kesî ti caran yanî ji me re gotiye.
 
and they haven't taken any, and no one has ever, meaning,
said it to us.

147
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Yanî malbat di yek in,
 
Meaning the families are one,

148
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Yanî malbata we û malbata wan?
 
Meaning your family and their family?

149
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Na ne yek in.
 
No, they are not one.

150
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Bes eynî Kurê Ehmed e.
 
But it's exactly Kurê Ehmed.

151
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Mala Opê me li Kurkê Jorîn in, em jî li Jêrîn in.
 
Our Opê family is in Upper Kurk, and we are in Lower.

152
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Û mala Opê me di jî, hin li Dimîla ne, ew esas jî bingeha
xwe li Badîna ye.
 
And our other Opê family, some are in Dimila, their actual
roots are in Badina.

153
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Naha di her gundekî de, berê kesên navdar hebûn...
 
Now, in every village, there used to be famous people...

154
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
kesên rûspî wan, kesên qehreman, kesên dengbêj.
 
their elders, heroic people, singers.

155
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Yanî li ba we kî heye?
 
I mean, who is there among you?

156
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Welleh, navdar,
 
By God, famous people,

157
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
dema gund heyder axa hebû.
 
when the village had Heyder Axa.

158
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Û êdî rûspîyên gund, pêşta wî,
 
And the village elders, beforehand,

159
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Hemedê Hesenê hebû,
 
there was Hemedê Hesenê,

160
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Hewsî Ebdîkê hebû,
 
Hewsî Ebdîkê was there,

161
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Xelîlê Hacî hebû,
 
Xelîlê Hacî was there,

162
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Mistê Ezîz hebû (Mixtarê gund bû),
 
Mistê Ezîz was there (he was the mukhtar of the village),

163
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Şikrê Heyder hebû, Ehmedê Hacî hebû.
 
Şikrê Heyder was there, Ehmedê Hacî was there.

164
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Vana çi tişt li gund, derdorê gund çêbûbûya,
 
Whatever happened in the village, around the village,

165
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,000
ev diketin meseleyê vana û tiştên wan hel dikirin,
 
they would intervene in these matters and resolve them,

166
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
nedihiştin anî tiştekî zirar jê çêbibe.
 
they wouldn't allow any harm to come from it.

167
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Û di gund de jî di aliyê şoreşê de,
 
And in the village, on the side of the revolution,

168
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
di aliyê welatparêziyê de du pakrewan hene.
 
on the side of patriotism, there are two martyrs.

169
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Yek bi navê Şehîd Dilşêr, yek bi navê Şehîd Cîhad.
 
One named Martyr Dilşêr, one named Martyr Cîhad.

170
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Komîna gund bi navê Şehîd Cîhad e,
 
The village commune is named after Martyr Cîhad,

171
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
û dibistana gund bi navê Şehîd Dilşêr e.
 
and the village school is named after Martyr Dilşêr.

172
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Gundê me, tiştekî pir balkêş tê de bû,
 
In our village, there was something very interesting,

173
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
yekîtî, dilrehmî û ruhekî welatparêziyê tê de hebû.
 
there was unity, compassion, and a spirit of patriotism.

174
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Di salên heftêyî de ermeniyên
 
In the seventies, the Armenians

175
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
koçber bibûn, ji serxetê hatin,
 
who had migrated, came from Above the Line (North
Kurdistan),

176
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
li Rojavayê me rûniştin.
 
and settled in our Rojava.

177
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Danûstandin di mabeyna gundiyên me û wan de pir baş bû,
 
The relationship between our villagers and them was very
good,

178
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
û weke cîranan jî zewicîn,
 
and as neighbors they also married,

179
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
hildan û dan hebû di navbera wan de.
 
there was intermarriage between them.

180
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,000
Ziyaretek li gund heye, du kaniyên avê lê hene.
 
There is a shrine in the village, there are two water
springs there.

181
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Yek jê, ji wan gundiyan çûye ew kanî girtiye.
 
One of them, one of those villagers went and built up that
spring.

182
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Û digotin Hemed ko ewî ava kir.
 
And they used to say Hemed built it.

183
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Ew jî li serê ereban da di başûrê gund de ye.
 
And that is above the Arabs in the south of the village.

184
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Û dîsa ez dubare dikim em televîzyona Ronahî,
 
And again I repeat, we to Ronahî television,

185
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:31,000
kenalê Ronahî bi tevî karmend û xebatkarên wê re,
 
to the Ronahî channel with all its staff and workers,

186
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:35,000
em pir spas dikin. Ji ber hatina we em pir kêfxweş bûn.
 
we thank you very much. Because of your coming we were very
happy.

187
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Û em dixwazin hûn pêş bikevin û her zêde bibin,
 
And we want you to progress and always grow,

188
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
serkeftî bin di jiyana xwe de.
 
and be successful in your life.

189
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Em jî spasiya te dikin, gelek spas.
 
We also thank you, thanks a lot.

190
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Inşaellah em ê derbasî gund bibin, em ê gund nas bikin.
 
God willing we will pass into the village, we will get to
know the village.

191
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Spasiya te dikin.
 
We thank you.

192
00:11:46,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Silav û rêz.
 
Greetings and respects.

193
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Gundê Kurka Jêrîn girêdayî navçeya Mabetê ya kantona Efrînê
ye.
 
The village of Kurka Jêrîn is connected to the Mabeta
district of the Afrin canton.

194
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Heft kîlometroyan li bakur rojavayê bajarokê Mabetê,
 
Seven kilometers northwest of the town of Mabeta,

195
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
û bîst û du kîlometroyan li bakurê Efrînê dikeve.
 
and 22 kilometers north of Afrin.

196
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Gundê Kurka, li herêmê ku bi navê Kurka tê naskirin, hatîye
avakirin,
 
The village of Kurka is built in the region known as Kurka,

197
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:22,000
ku ew dever ji gundê Qopê li bakur, ta gundê Hemo li başûr,
bi navê xwe bi dawî dibe,
 
which extends from the village of Qopê in the north, to the
village of Hemo in the south, ending with its name,

198
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,000
lewma navê gund bûye Kurka.
 
therefore the name of the village became Kurka.

199
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Di serî de du bira li gund hebûn.
 
Originally, there were two brothers in the village.

200
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Yek li gundê Kurka Jorin, û yê din jî li gundê Kurka Jêrîn
niştecih bûn,
 
One settled in the village of Kurka Jorin, and the other in
the village of Kurka Jêrîn,

201
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
û her yekî gundek şên kir.
 
and each one populated a village.

202
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Gundê Kurka Jêrîn, gundekî kevnar e.
 
The village of Kurka Jêrîn is an ancient village.

203
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Tê gotin ku kesek bi navê Hemîd,
 
It is said that someone named Hemîd,

204
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
ji neviyên malbata yekemîn ku li gund ava kiribû heye.
 
from the descendants of the first family that built the
village, exists.

205
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:47,000
Lê wî bi sedema mirina kurekî xwe, ji gundê xwe bar kir,
 
But he, due to the death of his son, moved from his village,

206
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:51,000
cîhekî nediyar û naha kes şopa wê malbatê nizane.
 
to an unknown place and now no one knows the trace of that
family.

207
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Heştê û pênc xanî û derdora hezar kes li gund dijîn.
 
Eighty-five houses and around a thousand people live in the
village.

208
00:12:55,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Naha malbat koçî deverên dîtir bûne, û hin jî li bajarê
Efrînê niştecih bûne.
 
Now families have migrated to other areas, and some have
settled in the city of Afrin.

209
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Merheba dayê.
 
Hello mother.

210
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Merheba!
 
Hello!

211
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Rojbaş, xêr be?
 
Good day, how are you?

212
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Xêr û selamet be.
 
Goodness and peace to you.

213
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Merheba. Çawa yî dayê? Baş î?
 
Hello. How are you mother? Are you well?

214
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Baş im, baş im, sax û selametî be.
 
I'm well, I'm well, health and peace to you.

215
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Sax bî... Min dît tu zehmetê dikişînî, min xwest ez
sohbetekê bi te re bikim, em bi hev re rûnin.
 
May you be healthy... I saw you struggling, I wanted to have
a chat with you, let's sit together.

216
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Em çi bikin?
 
What should we do?

217
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Va çi didî hev? Va çi dikî tu?
 
What are you gathering? What are you doing?

218
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Em qotê daran, zeytûnan, ê me, kesê me tunene arî me bikin,
 
We gather twigs of trees, olives, we have no one to help us,

219
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
em biqelînin, zivistanê. Me got emê xwe bi agirî germ bikin.
 
to roast them, in the winter. We said we'll warm ourselves
with the fire.

220
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Yanî hun ji bo tenûrê alîkariyê dikin?
 
So you are helping out for the tandoor?

221
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Em ji agir re didin hev, em pê nan çêdikin, dikişînin.
 
We gather it for the fire, we bake bread with it, we pull
it.

222
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Ku hûn pê debara xwe bikin?
 
So you can make a living with it?

223
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Ya ehlen we sehlen, kerem bikin rûnin.
 
Welcome, welcome, please sit down.

224
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Sax bî... Dayê em nas bikin, navê te bi xêr?
 
Be healthy... Mother, let's get to know you, what is your
name?

225
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Navê min Fîdan.
 
My name is Fîdan.

226
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Ser çavan dayê. Tu ji vir î yan ne?
 
On my eyes, mother. Are you from here or not?

227
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Hemîdê.
 
Hemîdê.

228
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Ser çavan. Hûn di vî gundî de çi karî dikin?
 
On my eyes. What work do you do in this village?

229
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Welleh, îşte, em di nav zeytûnan de, darên zeytûna didin
hev.
 
By God, well, we are among the olives, we gather olive wood.

230
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Em dixebitin, xizmeta milkê xwe dikin.
 
We work, we take care of our property.

231
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Yanî çi tişt di gundê we de hene ku hûn pê mijûl bibin?
 
I mean, what things are in your village that you can be busy
with?

232
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Ê pez hebe, ga-çêlek hebe, mirov pê ve mijûl dibe. Em diçin
çolê...
 
If there are sheep, if there are cows and cattle, one is
busy with them. We go out to the fields...

233
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Têkiliyên di gundê we de baş in?
 
Are the relationships in your village good?

234
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Cîrantî mirov bi hev re alîkar be.
 
In neighborliness, people should help each other.

235
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Dema daniyan dikelînin, gundî çawa li derûdora hev kom
dibin, alîkariya hev dikin.
 
When they boil grains, how the villagers gather around each
other, they help each other.

236
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Yanî, mirov wisa bi hev re dibin alîkar. Her tiştîkî wisa
ye.
 
I mean, people help each other like this. Everything is like
that.

237
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Wê hebû.
 
It was there.

238
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Dayê, kaniyeke, min bîhîst, li gundê we de... navê wê çi ye?
 
Mother, a spring, I heard, in your village... what is its
name?

239
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Me bulxur dikeland, me li ser çila radexist.
 
We used to boil bulgur, we used to lay it out on cloths.

240
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Me derdora xwe didît cil di nav gund kom dikir.
 
We would look around and gather cloths in the village.

241
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Û me bulxurê xwe li ser radexist,
 
And we would spread our bulgur on it,

242
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,000
û carna ewr dibû, digirt baran, me kom dikir,
 
and sometimes it got cloudy, it rained, we would gather it,

243
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
me careke din çilên din, cil li ser dikir.
 
and again we would put other cloths, put cloths on top.

244
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Dema hişk dibû me ew vedikir
 
When it dried we would open it

245
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
me paqij dikir, paşê me dibir êr, (aş) me dihêra
 
we would clean it, then we would take it to the mill, we
would grind it

246
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
û me dikir çewal û datanî.
 
and we would put it in sacks and store it.

247
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Şelek jî?
 
Sacks too?

248
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Şelek jî.
 
Sacks too.

249
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Va şeleka te ji ku derê anîye? Şelekên we...
 
Where did you bring this sack from? Your sacks...

250
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Şelek, em diçûn navçeyê.
 
Sacks, we used to go to the district.

251
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Ev çiyayê li hember we, kîjan e?
 
This mountain opposite you, which one is it?

252
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Ê, ji gundê Qudeman, ji gundê Qudeman min anî.
 
Yes, from the village of Qudeman, I brought it from the
village of Qudeman.

253
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Tu çend sal e, tu li vî gundî bûk î?
 
How many years have you been a bride in this village?

254
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Çil û heşt sal, qey ne tenê de.
 
Forty-eight years, I think, not only that.

255
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Tu zû de ye!
 
You've been here a long time!

256
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Erê. Zû de ye.
 
Yes. It's been a long time.

257
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Dayê, naha, te kêrê xwe çêdikî?
 
Mother, now, do you do your own work?

258
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Îşte, dar û tiştan, çêdikim...
 
Well, wood and things, I do...

259
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Tu darên aşlê çêdikî?
 
Do you graft trees?

260
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Erê!
 
Yes!

261
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Tu kîjan daran aşlê dikî? Lê darê fistiqê...
 
Which trees do you graft? Well, the pistachio tree...

262
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
E, yê hinarê, ...
 
The pomegranate tree, ...

263
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:40,000
yê mişmişê (qeysî),
 
the apricot tree,

264
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:45,000
ê, ... ev darên bi fêkî, ez giştî aşlê dikim.
 
well, ... these fruit trees, I graft all of them.

265
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Naha di tiştekî de, ev hînbûna aşlêkirinê te ji kê dît?
 
Now in one thing, who did you learn this grafting from?

266
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Ez ji bavê xwe hîn bûm. Min pê re diçûm, wê wextê
 
I learned from my father. I used to go with him, at that
time

267
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Min dît ew çawa dikir, ez fêr bûm.
 
I saw how he did it, I learned.

268
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Û di nav gundê we de kî darên aşlê dikir? Li gundê we.
 
And in your village, who used to graft trees? In your
village.

269
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Jin an? Jin an mêr an?
 
Women? Women or men?

270
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
Kes nizane. Kî dikir...
 
No one knows. Who used to do it...

271
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Na, em nizanin kî dikir, ew kar ne kiriyê jinan bû.
 
No, we don't know who did it, that work was not women's
work.

272
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Naha, dayê tenê tu darên aşlê dikî?
 
Now, mother, do you only graft trees?

273
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Erê. Ez bi xwe dikim.
 
Yes. I do it myself.

274
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Naha li gundê we de, kî darên aşlê dikir, tu nizanî wekî
din?
 
Now in your village, who grafted trees, you don't know
anyone else?

275
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Welleh înan ez nizanim, yane kî wê aşlê dikir, kî nedikir.
 
By God, truly I don't know, who was grafting, who wasn't
grafting.

276
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Ê gundê me ji yê we cûda bû... min ji bavê xwe hîn kir.
 
Our village was different from yours... I learned from my
father.

277
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Te ji wî hîn bû?
 
You learned from him?

278
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

279
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Ser çavê me.
 
On our eyes.

280
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Çavê te sax bin.
 
May your eyes be healthy.

281
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Dayê, tu kanî ji min re, tiştekî, çîrokên kurmancî bêjî?
 
Mother, can you tell me something, some Kurdish stories?

282
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Ez, ez ji te re çîrokan bêjim?
 
Me, should I tell you stories?

283
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Em rûnin? Em rûnin ka.
 
Shall we sit? Let's sit.

284
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Çend xaniyên we hene dayê?
 
How many houses do you have mother?

285
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Xaniyê min? Du, sê xanî ne. Sê ne.
 
My house? They are two, three houses. They are three.

286
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Lê xewşa we, xaniyê we pir xweş e ha.
 
But your yard, your house is very nice.

287
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Ê baş e wisa.
 
It's good like this.

288
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Tiştên kelepûrî yê xelkê gundê tê de ne.
 
The heritage items of the village people are in it.

289
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Haa...
 
Haa...

290
00:16:50,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Tiştên kevin tê de pir in. Min bala xwe dayê. Em diçûn
nav... me berhev dikirin...
 
There are many old things in it. I noticed. We went
inside... we collected them...

291
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Em çûn. Ka dor û kaniya dorê hêjîrê...
 
We went. Let's look around the fig tree's spring...

292
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Li vir! Li jêr e.
 
Here! It's below.

293
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Ka em biçin. Ev çi ye?
 
Let's go. What is this?

294
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Dayê, tu berê, xwarina we çawa dikir?
 
Mother, in the past, how did you make your food?

295
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Em li derve, agir daxist,
 
We would make a fire outside,

296
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
dema pelên darên zeytûnê hişk dibûn, me tînan û me pê agir
dikir şîv çêdikir.
 
when the leaves of the olive trees dried, we brought them
and made a fire with them to cook dinner.

297
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Ev abeyê we kevin e?
 
Is this abaya of yours old?

298
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Erê kevin e. Me girtiye, îşte me... xwe re hilgirtiye.
 
Yes, it's old. We got it, well, we... kept it with us.

299
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Te bi xwe ra girt?
 
You kept it with yourself?

300
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

301
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Te ew kengî girt?
 
When did you get it?

302
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Ji kulfetiya xwe ve.
 
From my childhood.

303
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Haa... We kengî dest pê kir pê?
 
Haa... When did you start using it?

304
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Zû de.
 
A long time ago.

305
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Zû de... yanî ji mêj de ye.
 
Long ago... meaning it's from a long time ago.

306
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Ji mêj ve...
 
From a long time ago...

307
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Ka em rûnin.
 
Let's sit.

308
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Nene, ev hêjîra kê ye? Kîjan hêjîr e ev?
 
Grandma, whose fig is this? Which fig is this?

309
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Ev hêjîra kundirkî ye.
 
This is the kundirkî fig.

310
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Tê çi lê xî?
 
What do you do with it?

311
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Heke ez hêjîrê bixwim.
 
Only if I eat the fig.

312
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Na ev darê hêjîrê te ji ku anî.
 
No, where did you bring this fig tree from.

313
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Hêjîr e! Ev hêjîr e, hêjîra min e, ê min e ev. Ez giya didim
binê darên hêjîrê.
 
It's a fig! This is a fig, it's my fig, it's mine. I put
grass under the fig trees.

314
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Lê dayê, ev morke. Morkek, te ev mork xistiyê lê?
 
But mother, this bead. A bead, you put this bead on it?

315
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Morkên min in, min dixiste darên... ew tiştê dikim,
 
They are my beads, I would put them on trees... I make that
stuff,

316
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,000
ev tiştê ha dikim, dikim nav... dikelînim wek darê, evên
tişt dikim.
 
I do this thing, I put it inside... I boil it like a stick,
I do these things.

317
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Nerm, ev pûç e xirab e...
 
Soft, this is rotten, it's bad...

318
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Ev tişta reş çiye?
 
What is this black thing?

319
00:18:54,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Ev mû ye... reş e.
 
This is hair... it is black.

320
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Heta ez digihîştim vê derê, kela min pê radibû, ev riwek e.
 
Until I reached here, I would get angry, this is a plant.

321
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Reş û gewr bû, me tê de rûdinişt.
 
It was black and grey, we used to sit in it.

322
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Tu pê çi dikî?
 
What do you do with it?

323
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Ez palgehê jê çêdikim...
 
I make a cushion from it...

324
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Min ew didanî palgehên pîran, ev jê çêdikim...
 
I used to put it for the elders' cushions, I make this from
it...

325
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Tu wan... çawa, we bi çi dihûnand?
 
You... how, with what did you weave it?

326
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
Em reş dihûnin...
 
We weave it black...

327
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
We ev çi jê çêdikir?
 
What did you make out of this?

328
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Ê me ew bixwe dirist... we dizanîbû...
 
We used to spin it ourselves... you knew...

329
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Îşte ev banka gund e, çi dexl hebûna me dikir hundir.
 
Well this is the village bank, whatever grain there was we
put inside.

330
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
We lê zêde dikir?
 
Did you add to it?

331
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Na me lê zêde nedikir, me li ser hev datanî.
 
No we didn't add to it, we put it on top of each other.

332
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Germ e?
 
Is it warm?

333
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Germ.
 
Warm.

334
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
We lazût jî lê dikir?
 
Did you put corn in it too?

335
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Na.
 
No.

336
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Lazût nedikirinê?
 
They didn't put corn in it?

337
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Nedikirinê. Em çûn tiştan tînin...
 
They didn't. We went to bring things...

338
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Destê te sax bin dayê. Ê te ev sax bin.
 
Health to your hands mother. Yours too.

339
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Nana dayê di kîjan mehê de haşlar dikin?
 
Tell us mother, in which month do they make hashlar (boiled
figs)?

340
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Beriya ku bipeliqe, beriya ku hêjîr bipeliqin.
 
Before they ripen, before the figs ripen.

341
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Na na, dema haşlarkirinê. Dema hêjîrên haşlarkirî çêdikin,
nav kîjan mehê de çêdikin? Ne di payîzê de.
 
No no, when they boil them. When they make boiled figs, in
which month do they make them? Not in autumn.

342
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Hêjîrên biharê, baharê.
 
Spring figs, in the spring.

343
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Di çileyê de.
 
In winter (during the coldest period).

344
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Di çileyê de?
 
In winter?

345
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Di çileyê de an di sibatê de.
 
In winter or in February.

346
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Yanî, inşallah sala din em werin hêjîran bi te re bixwin.
 
I mean, God willing, next year we will come and eat figs
with you.

347
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Inşallah.
 
God willing.

348
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Em werin dar mezin bibin em hêjîra bixwin.
 
We'll come when the trees grow and eat figs.

349
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Inşallah, inşallah.
 
God willing, God willing.

350
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Destê te sax bin.
 
Health to your hands.

351
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Destê te jî sax bin, ser çavên min re hatin.
 
Health to your hands too, you came on my head and eyes (you
are very welcome).

352
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Mala te ava be.
 
May your house be prosperous.

353
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Xwedê kemasiya we nede. Xwedê we biparêze. Xwedê stargehekê
bide we. Xwedê alîkarê we be.
 
May God not let you lack anything. May God protect you. May
God give you shelter. May God be your helper.

354
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Sax bî, spas ji te re. Xatirê te.
 
Stay healthy, thank you. Goodbye.

355
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Ser sera ser çavan. Xatirê we.
 
You're very welcome. Goodbye.

356
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Em ê çêkin gundên dîlan û xemlan,
 
We will build villages of hearts and adornments,

357
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Ji dil derxin kovan û xeman,
 
Remove sorrows and worries from the heart,

358
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Bi xwîna xeman rê vekin ji kelaman,
 
With the blood of worries, open the way for words,

359
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Em ê bêjin em ê çêkin em ê lêxin,
 
We will say, we will build, we will strike,

360
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Xwînav bikin kevin û şopan ji kelexan,
 
Bathe in blood the old traces from the corpses,

361
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:55,000
Dijminê hov ji welatê xwedê derxin,
 
Drive the savage enemy out of God's land,

362
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:00,000
Dijminê hov ji welatê xwe derxin.
 
Drive the savage enemy out of our land.

363
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Li ser axa ku bi xwînê vê bel bû de,
 
Upon the land that is covered in blood,

364
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Li ser gula ku bi xwînê wê pel bû de,
 
Upon the flower whose petals are stained with blood,

365
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Li ser roja ku bi sibeheke tarî jî bû de,
 
Upon the day that even had a dark morning,

366
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Em ê bêjin em ê çêkin em ê lêxin,
 
We will say, we will build, we will strike,

367
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Hû ava bikin, kevneşopê jê kelêxin,
 
Build it all, boil away the old traditions,

368
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:38,000
Dijminê hov ji welatê xwe derxin.
 
Drive the savage enemy out of our land.

369
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:43,000
Dijminê hov ji welatê xwe derxin.
 
Drive the savage enemy out of our land.

370
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Li ser hêsirên di çavan de sekinîne,
 
Upon the tears lingering in the eyes,

371
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Li ser çavên di benda me qerimîne,
 
Upon the eyes that have grown weary waiting for us,

372
00:22:54,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Li ber dayikên li ber dîwaran rûniştîne,
 
For the mothers sitting by the walls,

373
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Em ê bêjin em ê çêkin em ê lêxin,
 
We will say, we will build, we will strike,

374
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Hû ava bikin, kevneşopê jê kelêxin.
 
Build it all, boil away the old traditions.

375
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:25,000
Li rojavayê gund Zeviya Zeytûnan a bi navê Ser Şikeftê,
 
To the west of the village is the Olive Field named Ser
Shikefte,

376
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Li başûr gundê Sariya, Kurka Jêrîn û riya diçe Efrînê,
 
To the south is Sariya village, Lower Kurka, and the road
leading to Afrin,

377
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Li rojhilatê gund Çeqelê Hekarê û Zeviyê Ser Xol,
 
To the east of the village is Cheqele Hekare and the Ser
Khol Field,

378
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Li bakur gundê Hopka û gundê Dîmiliya.
 
To the north are Hopka village and Dimiliya village.

379
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:43,000
Li rojavayê gund, Gola Qirka heye, wekî gola ku av lê kom
dibû, şêniyên gund jê re digotin seheta avdanan.
 
To the west of the village is Qirka Lake, a lake where water
gathered, the villagers called it the irrigation spot.

380
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Li başûrê gund Serdanga Hemûrad dikeve û li wir du bîrên avê
hene.
 
To the south of the village lies the Hemurad Shrine, where
there are two water wells.

381
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Goristana Dimiliya li rojhilatê gund e, beriya mezelên naha
ew gund avabûn.
 
Dimiliya Cemetery is to the east of the village; those
villages were built before the current graves.

382
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:57,000
Piştî komkujiya Ermeniyan di şerê cîhanê yê yekemîn de,
 
After the Armenian genocide during the First World War,

383
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:01,000
Yek ji mêrên gund bi jineke ermenî re zewicî,
 
One of the men of the village married an Armenian woman,

384
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Û çend ermenî jî li bakurê gund kargeheke hesinkariyê saz
kirin,
 
And several Armenians established a blacksmith workshop in
the north of the village,

385
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:26,000
Ta dema ku li gund bûn, pêşiya ku koçî bajarê Helebê bibin.
 
Until the time they were in the village, before they
migrated to the city of Aleppo.

386
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Merheba ciwano.
 
Hello young men.

387
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Merheba ehlen wesehlen.
 
Hello, welcome.

388
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Sax bin, kuro çawan in, wê em nas bikin?
 
Stay healthy, how are you guys? Can we get to know you?

389
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Em li silav û xêrhatinê ne, ser seran û ser çavan hûn hatin.
 
We greet and welcome you, you have come upon our heads and
eyes.

390
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Her çend perçe perçe kirine, Kurdistan e. Ser serê me, ser
çavê me hatin. Înşallah serkeftin para we ye.
 
No matter how much they divide it into pieces, it is
Kurdistan. You have come upon our heads and eyes. God
willing, success is your share.

391
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Sax be, em we nas bikin?
 
Stay healthy, can we get to know you?

392
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Mihemed navê min e.
 
My name is Mihemed.

393
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Ser çavan Apê Mihemed. Em te jî nas bikin?
 
Upon our eyes, Uncle Mihemed. Can we get to know you too?

394
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Navê min jî Ehmed e.
 
My name is Ehmed.

395
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:53,000
Ser çava Apê Ehmed.
 
Upon our eyes, Uncle Ehmed.

396
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Em destpêkê ji we dest pê bikin.
 
Let's start with you first.

397
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Naha em ji gund derketin, geliyekî li vir heye û ev der hemî
zinar e.
 
Now we came out of the village, there is a valley here and
this whole place is rocky.

398
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,000
Ka ev geliyê li vir ê dibêjinê çi?
 
Tell us, what do they call this valley here?

399
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Ev zinarê tê binavkirin bi navê Zinarê Şiyê.
 
This rock is called Zinarê Shiye (The Rock of Shiye).

400
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Zinarê kûçeyê. Ji çendekê şûnda ermenî hatin ve derê.
 
The rock of the street. After some time, Armenians came to
this place.

401
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Wê çaxê tevir, das, bîr tiştan çêkirin...
 
At that time, they made things like pickaxes, sickles, and
spades...

402
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:25,000
Hatin ve derê, ev derê jê re vekirin û dikanê xwe xistin.
 
They came here, opened this place for themselves, and set up
their shop.

403
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Bi çi navî tê naskirin ev der?
 
By what name is this place known?

404
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Ev tê naskirin Xirabê Tamirciyan.
 
This is known as Xirabe Tamirciyan (Ruins of the Repairmen).

405
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Xirabê...?
 
Ruins of...?

406
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Xirabê Tamirciyan.
 
Ruins of the Repairmen.

407
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Piştî wê dehan sal, panzdeh salan wan karên xwe kirin li ve
derê û rabûn çûn...
 
After that, for ten years, fifteen years, they did their
work here and then packed up and left...

408
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Weke şûna ciyê wî din jî wan girt, dikan vekirin, ê ma
nezanî.
 
Just like they took the place of another place, they opened
shops, then the rest is unknown.

409
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Apê Ehmed, ev der naha wek xirabeyekê maye, yanî zinar e.
 
Uncle Ehmed, this place has now remained as a ruin, meaning
it's rocky.

410
00:25:54,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Xirabe ye lê di vir de bîr hene. Yên me bûn me av jê
derdixist pezê xwe pê av dida.
 
It is a ruin, but there are wells in here. They belonged to
us, we used to draw water from them and water our sheep with
it.

411
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Hem şev û rojan, dewar û pez me pê av didan.
 
Both day and night, we used to water cattle and sheep with
them.

412
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Û qederekî xwe derbas kirin ji vir derketin çûn, gundiyan
xanî û kel û pelên wan şikandin.
 
And they spent a certain time, left from here, and the
villagers broke their houses and belongings.

413
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Li çend odeyî pêk dihat ev cih?
 
How many rooms did this place consist of?

414
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Wekî deh yanzdeh ode hebûn wextekî milet vir bûn...
 
There were about ten to eleven rooms when the people were
here...

415
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Deh ode hebûn ha?
 
There were ten rooms, huh?

416
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Deh yanzdeh ode bûn vir ha. Ciyê karê wan jê, hesinkariyê
ciyê xwe jê bûn.
 
There were ten to eleven rooms right here. Their workplace,
their blacksmith area was right there too.

417
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Li vir dikan dikirin.
 
They had their shop here.

418
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,000
Di nav yek cihî de bûn, mal û dikana kar?
 
Were they in the same place, the house and the work shop?

419
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Yek cî bûn dikan û kar xwe dikan rûniştine wek yekê bûn.
 
They were in one place, their shop and work, their residence
and shop were as one.

420
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Bîrên avê li cem hev bûn. Ew kesên ermen ji destê zilma
Tirkan reviyan hatin vê derê.
 
The water wells were next to each other. Those Armenian
people fled from the oppression of the Turks and came here.

421
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Û eleqedarên wan bi gundiyan re gelekî xurt bû û dan û
standina wan baş bû.
 
And their relationship with the villagers was very strong,
and their mutual interactions were good.

422
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Nêzîkî deh panzdeh salan li vê derê man.
 
They stayed here for about ten to fifteen years.

423
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Û piştre çûn ku derê?
 
And then where did they go?

424
00:26:55,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Piştre laşê wan û kûde çûn nizanim wekî, kes nizane, û sebeb
jê heye.
 
Then I don't know where their bodies and where they went, no
one knows, and there is a reason for it.

425
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Sebebê çûna wan çi bû?
 
What was the reason for their departure?

426
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Sebebê çûyîna wan wisa bû ku li ser kûmre pev çûn.
 
The reason for their departure was that they fought over
charcoal.

427
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,000
Ji bo çi ew kûmr dihat bikaranîn?
 
What was that charcoal used for?

428
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Ew kûmr dişewitandin daku hesin pê germ bikin. Hesin germ
dikirin û difetisandin.
 
They burned that charcoal so they could heat iron with it.
They would heat the iron and mold it.

429
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Apê Mihemed wê wextê gundî çawan pê ra debara xwe dikirin?
 
Uncle Mihemed, how did the villagers make a living with them
at that time?

430
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:34,000
Ev der di dest wan de bûn. Ew li vî gundî jiyan. Gund û wan
yek bûn, jinek jî li vir hebû me dît em jê re digotin
Sultan.
 
This place was in their hands. They lived in this village.
The village and them were one, there was also a woman here
we saw, we used to call her Sultan.

431
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Jinik gundî bû?
 
Was the woman a villager?

432
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Belê jina vî gundî bû rehma xwedê lê be, nav gundê xwe de
dijiya, ew bi xwe qîza malên vir bû her tişt dikir.
 
Yes, she was a woman of this village, may God have mercy on
her, she lived in her village, she herself was a daughter of
the homes here, she did everything.

433
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:47,000
Qîza qîzeke gundiya bû.
 
The daughter of a village girl.

434
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:50,000
Piştî ku ew çûn, ti carî venegeriyan vir?
 
After they left, did they never return here?

435
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Na, nehatin û venegeriyan li wexta me nehatin jê.
 
No, they didn't come and didn't return, in our time they
didn't come.

436
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
Çûn Helebê, yan çûn Efrînê?
 
Did they go to Aleppo, or did they go to Afrin?

437
00:27:56,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Pêşî çûn Helebê, paşê çûn Efrînê belê em bi temamî nizanin
kû çûn. Ev qas me bihîst em we nizanin.
 
First they went to Aleppo, then they went to Afrin, but we
don't completely know where they went. We only heard this
much, we don't know the rest.

438
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Di wê demê de gelek milletê Ermeniyan berê xwe dan Rojavayê
Kurdistanê.
 
At that time, many Armenian people headed to Western
Kurdistan (Rojava).

439
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Hinek hatin Efrînê, hinek çûn Kobanê, hinek çûn Cizîrê,
 
Some came to Afrin, some went to Kobani, some went to
Cizire,

440
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:17,000
Lê li Efrînê jî hê heta niha jî malbatên ermenî hene,
 
But in Afrin, even up to now, there are still Armenian
families,

441
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Mînak, li gundê Heçqelî heya niha ermenî hene.
 
For example, in the village of Hechqeli, there are Armenians
to this day.

442
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Wexta dema ew ji zilma Tirkan reviyan û hatin vir, wê demê
ne em bûn yanî me bi çavên xwe ne dîtine bûn.
 
At the time when they fled the oppression of the Turks and
came here, we were not there, meaning we had not seen them
with our own eyes.

443
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:39,000
Hinek heta berî demeke nêzîk li Efrînê dikanên wan hebûn, me
ev didîtin, ew li efrînê xwedî cî û dikana bûn.
 
Some of them, until recently, had shops in Afrin, we used to
see this, they owned places and shops in Afrin.

444
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Navê yek ji wan Hagop bû me nas dikir...
 
The name of one of them was Hagop, we used to know him...

445
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Apo Ehmed em pirs bikin.
 
Uncle Ehmed, let us ask.

446
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Ev gelî navê vî ye geliyê Zeytûnan? Kîjan gund li derdora wî
hene?
 
Is this valley named the Valley of Olives? Which villages
are around it?

447
00:28:53,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Gundê li vê derê, pêşî ev der Geliyê Reş û Geliyê Zeytûnan
e, yan jê re dibêjin Geliyê Hoppo.
 
The villages here, first of all this place is the Black
Valley and the Valley of Olives, or they call it the Valley
of Hoppo.

448
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Gundên weke, Sariya, Gundê Qitmê, ta digihîje gundê Xelîl,
hemî li vê derdorê ne.
 
Villages like Sariya, Qitme Village, all the way reaching to
Xelil Village, they are all in this vicinity.

449
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Hemî ev gund bi hev re nêzîk bûn û di nav ahenga baş de bûn.
Der û dor hemî baş bi hev re bûn, we dît ku ev der mezin
bûn.
 
All these villages were close together and in good harmony.
The surroundings were all good together, you saw that these
places grew.

450
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:35,000
Dema em hemî bi hev re bûn, tevlihev me alîkariya hevdû
dikir me xatirê hev digirtin di wan deman de, wek misilman
em bira bûn, wek gundî tev pêre bûn...
 
When we were all together, all mixed, we used to help each
other and respect one another in those times, as Muslims we
were brothers, as villagers everyone was together...

451
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Apê Ehmed, di dawiyê de çi hêviya we, daxwazeke we derbarê
vî gundî de heye?
 
Uncle Ehmed, finally, what hope or wish do you have
regarding this village?

452
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Bi xwedê min dixwest gundê xwe, dîsa xelkê wî werin tê de
rûnin, aram bibe.
 
By God, I wanted my village, for its people to come and
settle in it again, for it to become peaceful.

453
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:59,000
Hêviya me em wextek xweş li gundê xwe, li ser axa xwe derbas
bikin, careke din em rûnin di ciyê xwe de bibin xwedî
îstiqrar li vir.
 
Our hope is to spend a good time in our village, on our
land, to once again settle in our place and find stability
here.

454
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Spas Apê Ehmed. Spas Apê Mihemed. Sax bin.
 
Thank you Uncle Ehmed. Thank you Uncle Mihemed. Stay
healthy.

455
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Gelekî çû xwar, baranê lê dixist. Qet ev gelî, wisa, dihat,
ev geliyên din zû tê.
 
It went down a lot, the rain was hitting it. This valley,
like this, came, these other valleys come early.

456
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Berê, berfa pir lê dikir?
 
Did it snow a lot in the past?

457
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Berf? Ti bîrêt te, dema em... berf... digotin 40 berf e.
 
Snow? Do you remember, when we... snow... they used to call
it the 40 snow.

458
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Çil berf e, dihat, rehmetî, rehmet li miriyê te be, xaniyê
me xaniyê me heta vî reşî kir, em di ser re doxirî diçûn
avê.
 
It was 40 snows, it came, the late, God's mercy on your dead
ones, our house was covered up to this black mark, we used
to walk straight over it to the water.

459
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Ya an jî car hebû berf çil berf dihat piştre xanî diqelişî
bû.
 
Or sometimes there was snow, 40 snows would come, then the
house would crack.

460
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Em di ser berfê re diçûn ser xênî. Du sale wisa nîne.
 
We would walk over the snow onto the roof. It hasn't been
like that for two years.

461
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Çend sal bû ev rû da tu dîtî? Dîroka xwe dizanî tu dî?
 
How many years ago did this happen that you saw? Do you know
the date when you saw it?

462
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Na em digotin 40 berf hebû, me nas dikir 40 berf hebû.
 
No, we used to say there were 40 snows, we knew there were
40 snows.

463
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Li vir darên...?
 
Are there trees here...?

464
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Li vir darên mezin hebûn. Zinar qelaştibû bi emrê Xwedê.
Şevê qelaşt, em çûbûn wir.
 
There were big trees here. The rock split by God's command.
It split at night, we had gone there.

465
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:52,000
Em diçûn, çil du metro kûr e.
 
We used to go, it is forty-two meters deep.

466
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Xuş xuş xuş... bîn, binê wê, dengê avê tê, av dihat.
 
Swoosh swoosh swoosh... below, under it, you could hear the
sound of water, water was coming.

467
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Lê çiyane em nizanin.
 
But we don't know what kind of mountains.

468
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:09,000
Av diherikî, em binê wê nedidîtin. Bermîlek av de rêt, yek
lefek darek avêt, sê çar qalikên fistiqan de rêtin.
 
Water was flowing, we couldn't see the bottom. They poured a
barrel of water in it, one threw a piece of wood, poured
three or four pistachio shells.

469
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:14,000
Avêtin wir, av ji kîjan alî de diçe. Lê nizanin, nizanin. Ji
kîjan alî de diçe nizanin.
 
They threw them there, to see which way the water goes. But
they don't know, they don't know. They don't know which way
it goes.

470
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Li vir sarnîcê avê jî hene?
 
Are there also water cisterns here?

471
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:20,000
Sarnîcên avê der û doran de hene. Li van deran tune ne.
 
There are water cisterns around here. There aren't any in
these places.

472
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Li kû derê?
 
Where?

473
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Di binê geliyê Sarnîcê. Li darê wê, geliyê Sarnîcê heye. Ev
sarnîcan me nedîtin, dibêjin geliyê Sarnîcan e.
 
Below Sarnic valley. At its trees, there is Sarnic valley.
We haven't seen these cisterns, they call it Sarnic valley.

474
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Ew nêzîkî gundê Mehmilo ye?
 
Is that near Mehmilo village?

475
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Na em diçin pişt wê, hinekî dûr e.
 
No, we go behind it, it's a bit far.

476
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:34,000
Geliyek heye, em jê re dibêjin geliyê Sarnîcan.
 
There is a valley, we call it the valley of Sarnic.

477
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Heta berê Sarnîc di nav de hebûn.
 
In the past there were cisterns in it.

478
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Û li vir jî te got cirnên kêlan e?
 
And here you also said there are hollowed stones?

479
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Erê, cirnê Tatkoyê.
 
Yes, the hollow of Tatko.

480
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Navê çi lê hatiye?
 
What is it called?

481
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Nav yekî got de kol e. Temen dirêj be dot avê ji bo ku xurt
bûye koliye koliye gotin cirnê kol e.
 
One said it's hollow. May you have a long life, he milked
water because he got strong, he dug it and dug it, they said
it's a hollowed stone.

482
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Ji gundiyan kî bû ye?
 
Who among the villagers was it?

483
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Heta halê niha gundiyê me ye, zora gund...
 
Even up to now he is our villager, mostly the village...

484
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Dibêjin cirnê kole.
 
They call it the hollowed stone.

485
00:31:57,000 --> 00:31:59,000
Em spasî ya te dikin. Saet xweş.
 
We thank you. Have a good time.

486
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Selamên min hene we re. Ser çavan. Spas xweş.
 
I send you greetings. You are welcome. Thank you.

487
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Şêniyê gundê Berajiya, nexweşiyên û xemanê xelkê dert û dorê
bi çandinî ya darên zeytûnê, wekî karê sereke dikin.
 
The residents of Berajiya village, despite the illnesses and
sorrows of the surrounding people, engage in olive tree
cultivation as their main job.

488
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Di gel wî çend malbat sewalên xwedî dikin.
 
Alongside this, several families raise livestock.

489
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:32,000
Nêzîkî pêncî û yekemîn nûjeyan li gund heye.
 
There are nearly fifty-one newly built houses in the
village.

490
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Tê de 60 kes dixebitin, û nêzîkî deh kes ji li bajarê Efrînê
di kargehên cor bi cor de dixebitin.
 
60 people work there, and nearly ten people also work in
various factories in the city of Afrin.

491
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Û nêzîkî bîst kes ji derveyî Sûriyê destkeftiyên rojane
xwedî dikin.
 
And nearly twenty people work outside Syria for their daily
livelihood.

492
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Her wiha di paqijrewan ji gund hene.
 
Also, there are martyrs from the village.

493
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,000
Şehîd Dilşêr, û Şehîd Cîhad.
 
Martyr Dilsher, and Martyr Jihad.

494
00:33:48,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Dibistana gund bi navê Şehîd Dilşêr e, û komîna gund jî bi
navê Şehîd Cîhad e.
 
The village school is named after Martyr Dilsher, and the
village commune is named after Martyr Jihad.

495
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja...
 
Yes, dear viewers...

496
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Îroj em li gundekî karkirin ne. Navê wî jî me da xuyanî kir
ku em ji ber vê gundî re meşîn...
 
Today we are in a working village. We have revealed its name
as we walked around this village...

497
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Ev hevalê me jî, navê te?
 
And this friend of ours, what is your name?

498
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Selah.
 
Salah.

499
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Selah. Tu başî, tu rind î?
 
Salah. Are you well, are you fine?

500
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,000
Baş e elhemdulilah.
 
Well, praise be to God.

501
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Tu ji kîjan alî de karê xwe xwedî dikî?
 
From which side do you manage your work?

502
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Welleh karê min ev gund e, em bere...
 
By God, my work is this village, we used to...

503
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Gundê me qismek elektrîkê e, faturên elektrîkê...
 
The name of the village?

504
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:33,000
Gundê me qismek elektrîkê e, faturên elektrîkê...
 
Our village is part of the electricity, electricity bills...

505
00:34:33,000 --> 00:34:38,000
Em mal bi mal digeriyan, her kesek li ser vî gundî me
didanîn pêşiyê.
 
We went from house to house, putting everyone in this
village forward.

506
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Û êdî, ez ji mêj ve dîroxa wê dinivîsim.
 
And well, I've been writing its history for a long time.

507
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:44,000
Tê de hemû, meblexê wan...
 
In it all, their amounts...

508
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Tu bi xwe nanivîsînî?
 
You don't write them yourself?

509
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Na tu neçûye dibistanê, mektebê, tu ne çûyî?
 
No, haven't you gone to school, haven't you gone?

510
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Çûme çûme bes, ez maneyê qelem... Ez me'na qelemê nizanim.
 
I went, I went but, I don't know the meaning of a pen... I
don't know the meaning of a pen.

511
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Her kes bi tarîxê xwe, ez mîşanî dikim.
 
Everyone by their history, I point them out.

512
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:58,000
Tarîxê ev meblex, û ev xwediye jî, ez dıdemî.
 
The date is this amount, and this is its owner, I give it.

513
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Naxwe Selah te çend sal nabînin?
 
So Salah, for how many years have you not been able to see?

514
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:04,000
Teqrîben 35 sal in.
 
Approximately 35 years.

515
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:07,000
35 sal in? Tu çend salî yî naha?
 
35 years? How old are you now?

516
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Ez 39 im.
 
I am 39.

517
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,000
39, Xwedê temenê te dirêj bike.
 
39, may God prolong your life.

518
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:15,000
Naxwe 35 sal in te nedî. Û çi nexweşiyek derbas bû ya çi bû
ev?
 
So for 35 years you haven't seen. And what disease happened
or what was it?

519
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Welleh ez çûçik bûm, omrê min 3, 4 salî bû, teqrîben...
 
By God, I was small, my age was 3 or 4 years old,
approximately...

520
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:23,000
Wekî taya xirab, wekî hema wextê nexweşiyek wisa hat.
 
Like a bad fever, like just a time such a disease came.

521
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Û, ev ma rewşa min, û berê jî doxtor-mixtor tunebûn, mualece
tunebûn. Hema ev ma rewşa min.
 
And this remained my condition, and in the past there were
no doctors, no treatments. This just remained my condition.

522
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Naxwe, li gund de behsa te dikirin, digotin, tu gelek karan
dikî.
 
So, they were talking about you in the village, they said
you do many things.

523
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Tu çi karî dikî? Yanî mextelê rasterast tê da defter di
destê te de?
 
Exactly.

524
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Tu çi karî dikî? Yanî mextelê rasterast tê da defter di
destê te de?
 
What jobs do you do? I mean, directly, you had a notebook in
your hands?

525
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Te lê dinêrî, te digerî?
 
Exactly.

526
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Te lê dinêrî, te digerî?
 
You were looking at it, searching through it?

527
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Tu heta wisa jî dinê, tu çi karan dikî?
 
Exactly.

528
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Tu heta wisa jî dinê, tu çi karan dikî?
 
Up to this point, what jobs do you do?

529
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Ez, wehdên jamxorê difroşim... tehwîl wehdat.
 
I sell top-up units... unit transfers.

530
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Megabayt... xet û... aliyê vir ê zeytûnê de.
 
Megabytes... lines and... in this area around olives.

531
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Zeytûnên reş, ez çêdikim.
 
Black olives, I prepare them.

532
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:57,000
Ez diçim dikirim... mehbezê dikim. Dîsa difroşim.
 
I go and buy them... I press them. Then I sell them again.

533
00:35:57,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Naxwe te wehdat çawa dişînin ye?
 
So how do you send the units?

534
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:02,000
Wehdat rasterast, ji telefona xwe dişînim.
 
The units directly, I send them from my phone.

535
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Telefona te heye?
 
Do you have a phone?

536
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Belê telefona min heye, ev telefon.
 
Yes, I have a phone, this phone.

537
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Bê berxwez ji telefonê, telefona te dibêje?
 
Without looking at the phone, your phone talks?

538
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Temam.
 
Exactly.

539
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,000
Kî telefona xwe bide te...
 
Who gives you their phone...

540
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Te çawa dişîneyî nimreya wî? Tu ji me re bibêje?
 
How do you send it to his number? Tell us?

541
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Temam.
 
Exactly.

542
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Tu bişînin, yek telefonê bîne? Numreya xwe ji min re bêje?
Temam.
 
You send, someone bring a phone? Tell me your number?
Exactly.

543
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,000
Tu dişînî?
 
Do you send?

544
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

545
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Te çawa dinivîse? Ka em lê binêrin çawa ye?
 
How do you write it? Let's see how it is?

546
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:25,000
Temam.
 
Exactly.

547
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:28,000
(Telefon: sê... sifir... sê... )
 
(Phone: three... zero... three...)

548
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Va ye, ev diçe sîstem.
 
Here, this goes to the system.

549
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:32,000
(Telefon: nehe...sê...pênc...)
 
(Phone: nine... three... five...)

550
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Ev reqemê min e, teben.
 
This is my number, naturally.

551
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:38,000
(Telefon: du... yek... pênc... heşt...)
 
(Phone: two... one... five... eight...)

552
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Ev heye reqemê min...
 
This is my number...

553
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Naxwe tu çawa dibirî? Ev telefona te ya yek heye wek wê tê
de hene?
 
So how do you manage? Does your single phone have features
like this?

554
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Temam.
 
Exactly.

555
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,000
Temam. Te çawa bîr dikir?
 
Exactly. How did you remember?

556
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Li wira... wekî niha te reqemê xwe didî min, 12, 33...
 
There... like now you give me your number, 12, 33...

557
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:57,000
Ka ji me re bi reqemê min bêje?
 
Could you tell me my number?

558
00:36:57,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Temam. Ka telefona xwe bide min?
 
Exactly. Can you give me your phone?

559
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Sifir... neh...
 
Zero... nine...

560
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:03,000
Sifir du neh...
 
Zero two nine...

561
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:03,000
Sê sê.
 
Three three.

562
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Sê sê.
 
Three three.

563
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Haft.
 
Eight...

564
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Haft.
 
Seven.

565
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Sifir.
 
Zero.

566
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Sifir.
 
Zero.

567
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Du neh... Sê sê...
 
Two nine.

568
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Du neh... Sê sê...
 
Two nine... Three three...

569
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:11,000
Heft şeş.
 
Seven six.

570
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:14,000
Heft şeş.
 
Seven six.

571
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Naxwe te çawa zanî? Te çawa zanî...
 
So how did you know? How did you know...

572
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:22,000
Lems e, ev nexşê telefonê..
 
It's touch, this map of the phone...

573
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Yanî ew nexşê wê te di eqlê xwe de girtiye.
 
Meaning you have memorized its map in your mind.

574
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:30,000
Bese ez nexşa 5 yan bese ez nexşa 2 zanim... Lê ektiriya
reqeman bi zehniya xwe min hifz kirine.
 
Maybe I know map 5 or maybe I know map 2... But most numbers
I have memorized mentally.

575
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:32,000
Dîsa, karê çi jî, cîhazekî te yî din jî heye?
 
Also, what else do you do, you have another device?

576
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:34,000
Cihazekî din nateqe, wisa nateqe.
 
The other device doesn't speak, it doesn't speak like this.

577
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:35,000
